{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1453969","title":"Responses of microbial communities in sewer sediment to HPAHs exposure","description":"Heterocyclic polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (HPAHs) are typical toxic and persistent organic pollutants accumulated widely in sewer sediments. Long-term HPAHs contamination exerts strong selective pressure on benthic microorganisms and inevitably alters microbial community structure, diversity, and ecological functions. In this study, high-throughput sequencing was used to characterize the composition and distribution of microbial communities in sewer sediments under different HPAHs exposure. The aim is to reveal the response patterns, community assembly processes, and potential functional changes of sediment microorganisms driven by HPAHs stress. This dataset provides fundamental microbial information for assessing ecological risks of HPAHs pollution and developing in-situ bioremediation strategies for sewer sediment in urban drainage systems.","center":"tongji university","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/04/15 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN57286051","Metagenome or environmental sample from sediment metagenome","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater","2024-12-02",2024,"CN","Shanghai",1796236,"Shanghai","verified",31.25,121.52,"China: Shanghai","Urban stormwater sewer sediment",null,null,null,"explicit urban setting at sample level"],["SAMN57286052","Metagenome or environmental sample from sediment metagenome","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater","2024-12-02",2024,"CN","Shanghai",1796236,"Shanghai","verified",31.25,121.52,"China: Shanghai","Urban stormwater sewer sediment",null,null,null,"explicit urban setting at sample level"],["SAMN57286053","Metage